  <event id="177">
      <start>10:30</start>
      <duration>00:45</duration>
      <room>H.1308</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>OpenSync</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>openSUSE</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;OpenSync - Synchronization Framework for mobile devices.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A short introduction of OpenSync, a Synchronization Framework. The Framework is intended to synchronize all kind of mobile devices, applications and &#xA;services. The talk includes some details about the features of the upcoming OpenSync 0.30 version.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://www.opensync.org/&#34;&gt;OpenSync&lt;/a&gt; is a Synchronization Framework. The framework is a desktop independent synchronization solution for all kind of mobile device and application. The plugin based architecture allows to enhance the support of new devices/protocols with providing a simple plugin. &#xA;There are so far OpenSync frontends for the command line, KDE and GNOME. At the moment framework supports: SyncML, IrMC and many other protocols and the KDE PIM and Evolution environment.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="1771">Daniel Gollub</person>
      </persons>
